  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The primary objective of the project is to strengthen the resilience and adaptive capacity of vulnerable communities and ecosystems in Malaysia by scaling up the use of Nature-based Solutions (NbS) and ecosystem-based adaptation (EbA) for integrated water resource management. The project targets three high-vulnerability landscapes: Peatlands (Selangor), Upstream Watersheds (Ulu Muda, Kedah), and Urban Ecosystems (Kuala Lumpur/Petaling Jaya). The project is designed around three mutually reinforcing components:</narrative>
  </description>
